Our architecture meets performance requirements, ensures data sovereignty, and provides an API interface. We have experience with Kubernetes, Docker, and SecNumCloud deployments, and our solution can be hosted on OVHcloud or Scaleway, both located in the European Union. We consider hosting the solution on a similar infrastructure to further enhance security and sovereignty.

Our company has a certification in ISO 27001, demonstrating our commitment to information security, and we comply with strict security protocols. We also have a green hosting partnership with OVHcloud and Scaleway, both using 100% renewable energy, reducing energetic consumption and relying on infrastructures with low carbon impact.

We propose a cost optimization strategy, with an annual operating cost compatible with the budgetary capacities of the local authority, and our gross margin percentage is 28.0%. The global budget for the project is estimated at 3 million euros over 4 years, and we will deploy the solution in a progressive manner, starting with a pilot phase on a limited scope and then progressively generalizing to all services.

Our solution contributes to reducing the environmental footprint of the city's IT systems, aligning with the city's policy of sustainable development. We provide training for agents, ensuring a smooth transition to the new system, and our evaluation criteria consider quality and relevance of the proposed solution, compliance to regulatory requirements, level of security, global cost of the proposed solution, taking into account environmental issues, and capacity of innovation.

In conclusion, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. proposes a comprehensive digital transformation solution that addresses the city's needs for improving administrative services efficiency and quality of service rendered to users, while ensuring compliance with regulatory requirements, data protection, and environmental sustainability.
